  "reason": "The pancyclic divergence theorem concerns only outerplanar graphs and a degree-constrained positive-integer weighted-tree model. The original minimum ranges over all pancyclic Hamiltonian graphs, including crossing chord systems; deleting crossing chords can destroy pancyclicity. Since h(n)<=h_out(n), a divergent lower bound on h_out does not supply the requested unrestricted lower bound. The sharp leading quadratic star-dual subclass construction and internal k\u00b2+4 endpoint repair do not bridge this gap. The original divergence and stronger coefficient-one iterated-log lower bound remain unresolved.",
